  "user_request_original": "Execute a Transfer Matrix Method optimization for a 30-layer planar dielectric stack on a Fused Silica substrate with Air incidence. Materials: Alternating HfO2 and SiO2 (Layer 1 = HfO2). Wavelength bands: 400-700 nm (Target: High Reflectance), 1530-1565 nm (Target: High Transmittance). Topology: Layers 1-12 and 17-30 are Bragg mirror layers; Layers 13-16 are defect cavity layers. Initialization: Layers 13-16 initialized to half-wave optical thickness at 1550 nm (d = 1550 / (2 * n)). Optimization Constraints: Apply a step size scaling factor of 0.5 to variables for layers 13-16. Apply an increased penalty weight in the objective function for layers 1-12 and 17-30 deviating from quarter-wave optical thickness at 550 nm. Total layer count fixed at 30. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, and thicknesses_nm. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 1530-1565 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1530–1565 nm; high reflection in 400–700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: reflection in 1530–1565 nm; transmission in 400–700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 30.",
